; status: legitimate error — a paper edge is a segment bundle (ADR 0014),
; so --cd & .c now resolves segments instead of hard-rejecting ("--cd is a
; paper edge, not a crease with segments"). This particular fold happens to
; hit a DIFFERENT, honest error: `map .a onto .b` mirrors the square exactly
; in half, so c and d land on the same table point and both halves of --cd
; are incident to .c in table space — a real geometric ambiguity, not a gap
; in edge support. See edge-bundle-select-c.bel / -d.bel for an unambiguous
; case proving the selector discriminates.
paper square
fold --v = map .a onto .b
fold map --cd & .c onto --v

; expect error "ambiguous"
